Wait — idempotent() returns ServiceResult<T> but stores body JSON. Let me define:

```java
private <T> ServiceResult<T> idempotent(String scope, String requestId, Object payload, Class<T> type, Supplier<ServiceResult<T>> action) {
    String hash = sha256(payload.toString());
    var existing = repo.findIdempotency(scope, requestId);
    if (existing.isPresent()) {
        IdemRow row = existing.get();
        if (!row.payloadHash().equals(hash)) {
            throw ApiException.conflict("IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT", "相同 requestId 携带不同参数");
        }
        return new ServiceResult<>(row.status(), readBody(row.body(), type));
    }
    ServiceResult<T> result = action.get();
    repo.insertIdempotency(scope, requestId, hash, result.status(), writeBody(result.body()), Instant.now(clock));
    return result;
}
```

Note: if action throws ApiException, no idempotency record stored — retries of failed requests re-execute. That's acceptable (common approach).

