No DB_CLOSE_DELAY → released when context closes (Hikari closes). 

Test clock: mutable clock via @TestConfiguration in a shared base class. I'll create:

- `src/test/java/com/example/starter/snow/MutableClock.java` — test helper
- `src/test/java/com/example/starter/snow/SnowTestConfig.java`? Use @TestConfiguration inside a base test class `BaseSnowTest` with @SpringBootTest + @AutoConfigureMockMvc + @Import. Actually simplest: one abstract base class annotated:

```java
@SpringBootTest
@AutoConfigureMockMvc
@Import(BaseSnowTest.TestClockConfig.class)
abstract class BaseSnowTest {
    static final Instant FIXED_NOW = Instant.parse("2026-01-10T12:30:00Z");
    static final MutableClock CLOCK = new MutableClock(FIXED_NOW);

    @TestConfiguration
    static class TestClockConfig {
        @Bean @Primary Clock testClock() { return CLOCK; }
    }

    @Autowired MockMvc mvc;
    @Autowired JdbcTemplate jdbc;
    @Autowired ObjectMapper om;

    @BeforeEach void clean() {
        jdbc.update("DELETE FROM idempotency_record");
        jdbc.update("DELETE FROM lift_decision");
        jdbc.update("DELETE FROM lift_confirmation");
        jdbc.update("DELETE FROM lift_review");
        jdbc.update("DELETE FROM reading_correction");
        jdbc.update("DELETE FROM closure_command");
        jdbc.update("DELETE FROM snow_reading");
        jdbc.update("DELETE FROM area");
        CLOCK.set(FIXED_NOW);
    }
}
```

